.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_FORMAT
The output format when no flag names one:
.BR json ,
.BR plain ,
.BR table ,
.B treemap
or
.BR ndjson .
It wins over the agent and CI variables below.
.TP
.BR CLAUDECODE ", " CODEX_THREAD_ID ", " CODEX_VERSION ", " GEMINI_CLI
Set by an agent's shell: the output is the JSON envelope, even on a
terminal.
.TP
.B CI
Set (and not
.B 0
or
.BR false ):
the output is
.BR \-\-plain .
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_CONFIG
The configuration file to read, as
.BR \-\-config ;
.B none
reads none.
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_INDEX_DIR
Where saved scans are kept, as
.BR \-\-index\-dir .
.TP
.BR SQLITE_TMPDIR ", " TMPDIR
Where a save puts SQLite's temporary sort file while it builds an index
(mode 0600, unlinked as it is opened); otherwise the first writable of
.IR /var/tmp ,
.IR /usr/tmp ,
.I /tmp
and the current directory.
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_THREADS
The scanner's worker threads, as
.BR \-\-threads .
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_THEME
The treemap's colours, as
.BR \-\-theme :
a pack's name or the path of a theme file.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set and not empty: no colour. The treemap is drawn in shades.
.TP
.BR CLICOLOR_FORCE ", " FORCE_COLOR
Set (and not
.B 0
or
.BR false ):
colour even when stdout is not a terminal.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
turns colour off.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
.B truecolor
or
.BR 24bit :
the treemap is drawn in 24\-bit colour; otherwise in the 256\-colour cube.
.TP
.B COLORFGBG
A light background (the last field 7 or 15) picks the light theme when
none is named.
.TP
.B LS_COLORS
The extension colours of
.BR "\-\-color\-by lscolors" .
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
Without UTF\-8 the treemap is drawn in ASCII.
.TP
.BR TMUX ", " STY
Set inside tmux and screen (as is a
.B TERM
of
.B tmux*
or
.BR screen* ),
which by default stop the sequence that sets the clipboard: the viewer's
.B y
leaves the clipboard alone there.
Inside tmux,
.B \-\-treemap pixels
draws the map in cells, with a warning, rather than change the pane's
settings to reach the terminal.
.TP
.B TERM_PROGRAM
.B Apple_Terminal
(macOS's Terminal, which takes no clipboard sequence) keeps the viewer's
.B y
from the clipboard as well, and
.B tmux
counts as inside tmux.
.TP
.B DUSCOPE_LOG
What is logged to stderr, in
.BR RUST_LOG 's
grammar: a level
.RB ( debug ),
a module
.RB ( duscope_walk ),
or both
.RB ( duscope_walk=debug ),
comma\-separated. A verbosity flag wins over it.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
As
.B DUSCOPE_LOG
when that is unset.
.TP
.B HOME
The home folder.
Under it are the index directory and the configuration file when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
and
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
are unset, and on Linux the home Trash when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is.
On macOS its
.I Library
is where a scan tries the Full Disk Access probe (see CAVEATS).
Its containers are what
.B \-\-skip\-containers
leaves out, a usage error without
.BR HOME .
.B explain
reads git's user configuration under it
.RI ( ~/.gitconfig ),
and the viewer writes it as
.I ~
in its header.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
The directory of saved scans,
.IR duscope/scans ;
.I ~/Library/Caches
on macOS and
.I ~/.cache
elsewhere when unset.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The directory of
.IR duscope/config.toml ;
.I ~/.config
when unset, on macOS too.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
On Linux, where the home Trash is,
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash ,
into which
.B clean
and the viewer move the items on the same filesystem;
.I ~/.local/share/Trash
when unset.
.TP
.B TZ
The local zone that
.BR \-\-since " and " \-\-until
read a date in.
